{
"opening": "This release marks the transition to version 1.0.0, introducing significant improvements to error handling, locale accuracy, and API precision while dropping support for older Python versions. The following requirements define the observable behavior of the public API that must be present in this release.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "The DateTimeParser class must raise a ParserError instead of a TypeError or re.error when string parsing fails to match specific patterns."
},
{
"id": "m05",
"text": "The JapaneseLocale must provide corrected translations for human-readable date and time strings to fix previous inaccuracies."
},
{
"id": "m06",
"text": "The Arrow.humanize method with granularity='auto' must apply more accurate limits to reduce unexpected results in time difference descriptions."
},
{
"id": "m07",
"text": "The library must no longer support Python 2.7 or Python 3.5, and all public names listed must reflect this environment constraint without exposing deprecated timestamp properties."
},
{
"id": "m09",
"text": "The library must correctly handle the maximum permitted timestamp on Windows systems by raising appropriate errors instead of failing silently or incorrectly."
},
{
"id": "m11",
"text": "The span, span_range, and interval methods must accept an 'exact' keyword argument that ensures timespans begin at the start time and do not extend beyond the end time."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "The Arrow class must expose a fromordinal method and the isoformat method must accept a timespec argument to control ISO 8601 output precision."
},
{
"id": "m19",
"text": "The ArrowFactory.get method must raise a TypeError when passed a None value as input."
}
]
}
